---
import Layout from '../layouts/WorkspaceLayout.astro'
import { WORKSPACE_VERSION, WORKSPACE_DOWNLOAD_URL, WORKSPACE_RELEASE_URL, WORKSPACE_SOURCE_URL, WORKSPACE_CHECKSUMS_URL, WORKSPACE_SHA256, WORKSPACE_CHATGPT_DOWNLOAD_URL, WORKSPACE_CHATGPT_SHA256 } from '../lib/workspace-release.mjs'
const prepareCommand = `uv sync --frozen --no-dev --project /absolute/path/to/veqtor-workspace-${WORKSPACE_VERSION}`
const connectionTimeouts = 'startup_timeout_sec = 180\ntool_timeout_sec = 330'
const firstPrompt = 'Use Veqtor Workspace to open the Word file at [paste the file location here]. Add a comment saying "Reviewed with Veqtor Workspace." Attach it to the first paragraph with text. Keep the document text unchanged. Save the result as a new file in the same folder, then tell me where it is.'
const launchCommand = `uv run --frozen --no-dev --project /absolute/path/to/veqtor-workspace-${WORKSPACE_VERSION} veqtor-workspace --author "Your Name"`
const launchArguments = `run\n--frozen\n--no-dev\n--project\n/absolute/path/to/veqtor-workspace-${WORKSPACE_VERSION}\nveqtor-workspace\n--author\nYour Name`
---
<Layout canonicalPath="/setup" title="Get started — Veqtor Workspace" description="Connect Veqtor Workspace to Claude Desktop or ChatGPT Desktop on your Mac. Try a small edit on a copy of a Word document.">
  <div class="shell setup-heading"><p class="concept-kicker">Installation</p><h1>Start with your AI assistant.</h1><p class="section-intro">Connect Veqtor on your Mac, then try one small change on a copy of a Word file.</p></div>
  <div class="shell setup-container" data-tabs>
    <div class="example-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Choose your assistant"><button type="button" role="tab" id="tab-claude" aria-controls="panel-claude" aria-selected="true">Claude Desktop</button><button type="button" role="tab" id="tab-chatgpt" aria-controls="panel-chatgpt" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">ChatGPT Desktop</button></div>
    <div role="tabpanel" id="panel-claude" aria-labelledby="tab-claude">
      <section class="setup-step"><span>1</span><div><h2>Download Veqtor for Mac</h2><p>You’ll need <a href="https://claude.com/download">Claude Desktop</a> installed and signed in. This installer is for Macs with Apple Silicon (M1 or newer).</p><a class="concept-button primary" href={WORKSPACE_DOWNLOAD_URL}>Download for Claude Desktop <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><p class="example-note">Version {WORKSPACE_VERSION} · Apple Silicon · M1 or newer · <a href={WORKSPACE_RELEASE_URL}>Release notes</a></p><details class="setup-details"><summary>Verify the download</summary><p>The <a href={WORKSPACE_CHECKSUMS_URL}>release checksums</a> identify the published installer. Its SHA-256 is:</p><div class="copy-container"><div class="copy-heading"><span>SHA-256</span><span data-copy-status role="status"></span><button type="button" data-copy="installer-checksum">Copy</button></div><pre id="installer-checksum">{WORKSPACE_SHA256}</pre></div></details></div></section>
      <section class="setup-step"><span>2</span><div><h2>Open it in Claude Desktop</h2><p>Open the downloaded file with Claude Desktop and choose Install. Enter the name you want used for new tracked changes and comments, then enable Veqtor Workspace.</p><p>No terminal commands or separate Python installation are needed. The first start downloads the required runtime and libraries; let it finish, then open a new chat.</p><p>Ask Claude whether it can see the Veqtor Workspace tools.</p></div></section>
      <section class="setup-step"><span>3</span><div><h2>Point to a saved copy</h2><p>Make a copy of a Word file with sample text. Save and close it in Word. In Finder, select the copy and press <kbd>⌥ ⌘ C</kbd> to copy its full location.</p><p>Paste that location into the request below. Veqtor uses the files you identify in your request.</p></div></section>
    </div>
    <div role="tabpanel" id="panel-chatgpt" aria-labelledby="tab-chatgpt" hidden>
      <section class="setup-step"><span>1</span><div>
        <h2>Download Veqtor for ChatGPT</h2>
        <p>You’ll need ChatGPT Desktop with local work enabled, a Mac with M1 or newer, and macOS 13 or newer.</p>
        <a class="concept-button primary" href={WORKSPACE_CHATGPT_DOWNLOAD_URL}>Download for ChatGPT Desktop <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
        <p class="example-note">Version {WORKSPACE_VERSION} · Apple Silicon · macOS 13+ · <a href={WORKSPACE_RELEASE_URL}>Release notes</a></p>
        <p><strong>This installer is not signed with Developer ID or notarized by Apple.</strong> macOS will ask you to allow it before it can open.</p>
        <details class="setup-details" open><summary>Allow the installer in macOS</summary>
          <p>Open the downloaded disk image and try to open Veqtor Workspace Setup. If macOS blocks it, go to System Settings → Privacy &amp; Security, find Veqtor Workspace Setup and choose Open Anyway. Confirm Open.</p>
          <p>Only allow the file downloaded from the official Veqtor release. <a href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/102445">Apple explains this permission</a>. A work-managed Mac may require your administrator’s approval.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="setup-details"><summary>Verify the download</summary><p>The <a href={WORKSPACE_CHECKSUMS_URL}>release checksums</a> identify both installers. The ChatGPT installer’s SHA-256 is:</p><div class="copy-container"><div class="copy-heading"><span>SHA-256</span><span data-copy-status role="status"></span><button type="button" data-copy="chatgpt-installer-checksum">Copy</button></div><pre id="chatgpt-installer-checksum">{WORKSPACE_CHATGPT_SHA256}</pre></div></details>
      </div></section>
      <section class="setup-step"><span>2</span><div>
        <h2>Click Connect to ChatGPT</h2>
        <p>Confirm the name you want used for new Word changes and comments, then click Connect to ChatGPT. Keep the installer open while it downloads and checks the required components.</p>
        <p>No terminal commands or manual connection settings are needed. The installer backs up your settings and adds Workspace while keeping your other connections and preferences.</p>
        <details class="setup-details"><summary>Manual setup for advanced users</summary>
          <p>If you prefer a manual connection, <a href={WORKSPACE_SOURCE_URL}>download the Workspace source</a>, unzip it to a permanent folder and install <a href="https://docs.astral.sh/uv/getting-started/installation/">uv</a>. Replace the example location with your folder, then run this once in Terminal:</p>
          <div class="copy-container"><div class="copy-heading"><span>First-time preparation</span><span data-copy-status role="status"></span><button type="button" data-copy="prepare-command">Copy</button></div><pre id="prepare-command">{prepareCommand}</pre></div>
          <p>In ChatGPT’s MCP settings, add a local STDIO server named Veqtor Workspace. Use <code>uv</code> as the command and these arguments, one per entry. Replace the folder and your name:</p>
          <div class="copy-container"><div class="copy-heading"><span>Arguments · one per line</span><span data-copy-status role="status"></span><button type="button" data-copy="launch-arguments">Copy</button></div><pre id="launch-arguments">{launchArguments}</pre></div>
          <p>In this server’s section of <code>~/.codex/config.toml</code>, add:</p>
          <div class="copy-container"><div class="copy-heading"><span>Connection timeouts</span><span data-copy-status role="status"></span><button type="button" data-copy="connection-timeouts">Copy</button></div><pre id="connection-timeouts">{connectionTimeouts}</pre></div>
          <p>Codex CLI and the IDE extension can use the same local command. See <a href="https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/extend/mcp">OpenAI’s connection instructions</a>.</p>
          <div class="copy-container"><div class="copy-heading"><span>Local launch command</span><span data-copy-status role="status"></span><button type="button" data-copy="launch-command">Copy</button></div><pre id="launch-command">{launchCommand}</pre></div>
        </details>
      </div></section>
      <section class="setup-step"><span>3</span><div><h2>Restart ChatGPT and choose a document</h2><p>After installation finishes, restart ChatGPT Desktop and start a new chat. An existing disabled Workspace connection stays disabled; enable it in ChatGPT’s MCP settings when you are ready.</p><p>Save and close a copy of a Word file. In Finder, select it and press <kbd>⌥ ⌘ C</kbd> to copy its full location. Paste the location into your request below.</p></div></section>
    </div>
    <section class="setup-step"><span>4</span><div><h2>Add your first comment</h2><p>Replace the bracketed text with the file’s location. This request adds one comment and saves a new file.</p><div class="copy-container"><div class="copy-heading"><span>Your first request</span><span data-copy-status role="status"></span><button type="button" data-copy="first-prompt">Copy request</button></div><blockquote id="first-prompt">{firstPrompt}</blockquote></div><p>Open the result in Word and check the comment and the document. For your next text edit, ask for tracked changes if you want to review each change.</p></div></section>
    <div class="setup-trouble"><h3>Before your first task</h3><div class="questions"><details><summary>Does this installer support Intel Macs?</summary><p>This installer requires Apple Silicon (M1 or newer). You can check your Mac’s chip in the Apple menu → About This Mac.</p></details><details><summary>What if Claude cannot install the extension?</summary><p>Use the current Claude Desktop app and open the downloaded file with it. If your organization restricts custom extensions, ask its administrator to allow Veqtor Workspace.</p></details><details><summary>I already use Veqtor MCP. Is this the same installer?</summary><p>Workspace is a separate product. The earlier installer and documentation remain available on the <a href="/veqtor-mcp">Veqtor MCP 0.5 page</a>. An existing Workspace preview updates in place when you install this extension.</p></details><details><summary>Can I keep editing in Word while the assistant works?</summary><p>Save first, and avoid editing the same file while the assistant saves it. Veqtor cannot read unsaved Word changes. If it updates a file that is still open in Word, reopen that file before continuing your manual edits.</p></details><details><summary>Do I need to write code?</summary><p>No. Both installers prepare the connection for you. Describe your document task in normal language. The ChatGPT installer needs the additional macOS permission explained above.</p></details><details><summary>Can I use confidential documents?</summary><p>Veqtor runs locally, but document content returned to the assistant becomes part of your AI conversation. Use documents only when processing them with your chosen AI service is permitted. Start with sample text.</p></details></div></div>
  </div>
</Layout>
